/* ==========================================================================
   Tarp726–825: a flexible chain with a partly prepared actin-binding helix.
   Meet Tarp and actin → converging evidence → NMR mapping → proposed complex.

   Actin surface: PDB 2A40 chain A, heavy atoms with van der Waals radii plus
   a 1.4 Å probe; a fixed orthographic solvent-accessible envelope. The WH2
   helix in chain C sets the view and cleft position only. Tarp is schematic,
   not a recovered docking model.

   Evidence tracks are approximate values read from the vector graphics of
   Fig. 2 and Supplementary Fig. S5, not the original numerical datasets.
   Error bars are omitted for legibility. HSQC positions and small shifts are
   approximate readings of Fig. S7; weakening dominates, as in the paper.
   Molecular motion illustrates states, not a measured binding pathway.
   ========================================================================== */
